# The scripted validators of the rewards demo, run
# by programs/validators. Each line is one act in one on-chain round:
#   round validator target score   the validator votes score on target
#   round validator opt-in         the validator opts itself in
# V1 to V4 have stake from round 3: V1 5,000 LPT (1,000 its own, 4,000 H's),
# V2 3,000, V3 2,000 and V4 6,000. V1 to V3 opt in in round 3 and are
# members from round 4. Their votes stand until replaced, so the claims read
# them: N 1,000,000 (nobody votes on it), M 500,000 (V1 and V2 vote 500,000),
# L 1,000,000 (V1 alone votes 0: one vote cannot cut a node) and K 0 (V1 and
# V2 vote 0).
3 V1 opt-in
3 V2 opt-in
3 V3 opt-in
4 V1 M 500000
4 V2 M 500000
4 V1 K 0
4 V2 K 0
4 V1 L 0
# V4 opts in in round 4 and takes the seat of V3, the smallest member, from
# round 5 (ValidatorSetSize is 3). Its vote in round 4 is refused
# NOT_VALIDATOR: it is not a member of round 4.
4 V4 opt-in
4 V4 K 0
